From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wlan: gen4m: Report a failed roam as a disconnection

When the driver loses the AP while connected (beacon timeout) it tries to
join another BSS itself. If that join fails it reports the failure with
cfg80211_connect_result(), as for a connect the host asked for. cfg80211
then drops the SSID but stays connected, so every later connect gets
-EALREADY, and the disconnect wpa_supplicant sends to clear it never
reaches the driver: Wi-Fi cannot reconnect until the module is reloaded.

Report the failure with cfg80211_disconnected() when cfg80211 holds a
connection.

---
--- a/wlan_drv_gen4m_6789/os/linux/gl_kal.c
+++ b/wlan_drv_gen4m_6789/os/linux/gl_kal.c
@@ -2119,7 +2119,17 @@
 			COPY_MAC_ADDR(arBssid,
 				prConnSettings->aucBSSID);
 		}
-		if (prBssDesc && prBssDesc->u2JoinStatus
+		if (prDevHandler->ieee80211_ptr->connected) {
+			/* The join that failed was a roam: the link is gone.
+			 * A connect result would leave cfg80211 connected and
+			 * refusing every later connect with -EALREADY.
+			 */
+			DBGLOG(INIT, WARN,
+			       "JOIN Failure while connected: disconnect\n");
+			cfg80211_disconnected(prDevHandler,
+				WLAN_REASON_UNSPECIFIED, NULL, 0, TRUE,
+				GFP_KERNEL);
+		} else if (prBssDesc && prBssDesc->u2JoinStatus
 		    && prBssDesc->u2JoinStatus != STATUS_CODE_AUTH_TIMEOUT
 		    && prBssDesc->u2JoinStatus != STATUS_CODE_ASSOC_TIMEOUT)
 			cfg80211_connect_result(prDevHandler,
